            <ArticleTitle>Neonatal pain and oxidative stress.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neonatal analgesia is a recent issue: newborns were supposed to feel no pain until the late &quot;80s; but from that date, many studies were performed to verify the extent of neonates&quot; pain perception, ways to measure and overcome it. Pain can have harmful consequences in babies, due to several causes, and we investigated whether oxidative stress can play a role in this process. Here we resume our findings, that recall to a greater safeguard of babies from unjustified pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
